Falsifies `capability_manifest_note::verification::an_inverted_memory_grant_does_not_encode`.

The defect: `encode` stops asserting that a required memory grant's minimum is no greater than its
maximum. A program could then build a note from such a manifest, and the reader would refuse that
note at run time, with nothing said at build time.

Expected to fail: the harness expects a panic and none comes.

diff --git a/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs
index b61755828..eca04bc2d 100644
--- a/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs
@@ -340,10 +340,6 @@ pub const fn encode(m: &Manifest) -> [u8; DESCRIPTOR_BYTES] {
         ProgramArgumentDeclaration::Words(WordGrant::Create) => 4,
     };
     if let MemoryGrantDeclaration::Required { minimum, maximum } = m.memory_grant {
-        assert!(
-            minimum <= maximum,
-            "a required memory grant has a minimum no greater than its maximum"
-        );
         out[MEMORY_GRANT] = 1;
         put8(&mut out, MEMORY_MINIMUM_PAGES, minimum);
         put8(&mut out, MEMORY_MAXIMUM_PAGES, maximum);
